      "content": "that makes sense. but when u say they both rely on \"textual interpretations\" and \"oral traditions,\" it sounds almost like they're just telling stories. from a historical or legal standpoint, though, is there one side that actually has a more valid or recognized claim? like, if we look at international law or actual historical documentation, does one side's argument hold more weight than the other? i just to be explain why one is more legitimate",
